      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Hodstock Hills [zone=1358]\n**Who:**\n- Captain Teiya [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 110\n**Maximum Level:** | 130\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Arcanist Aunrae V`Len [npc=60254]\n- Therok [npc=59985]\n- a decaying minion [npc=60218]\n- despair [npc=60260]\n- dread - ToB [npc=60261]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Partisan of Hodstock Hills (15 Points) [quest=13040]\n- The Best Defense... [quest=12985]\n**Era:** | !The Outer Brood\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Fri Oct 11 02:14:14 2024\nModified: Sun Jan 12 19:35:41 2025 | | You can obtain this task from Captain Teiya in Hodstock Hills. She is located in the northwestern corner of the zone near /way 1870, 2299, 484. She is on the find tool CTRL F.\nYou say, 'Hail, Captain Teiya'\nCaptain Teiya says, 'Vasha, \\_\\_\\_\\_, and well met. Welcome to Wyrmqueen's Ridge. Claw, Scale, and Wing have come together for the defense of Veeshan's claim. Are you here to also help [defend] her land?'\nYou say, 'I will defend Norrath.'\nCaptain Teiya says, 'Very good. Karui.' She looks over the adventurer, appraising the ability of the Dark Elf. 'As a fresh recruit, I have an initial assignment for you. Before I go into it, I will remind you that if you are here with only the intent for bloodshed, you will want to see Sergeant Malachi. My asks are a little more... nuanced. Do you [understand]?''\nYou say, 'I understand.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Mysterious Towers'.\nCaptain Teiya says, 'Karui.' She takes another pause, a rather uncomfortable length as she stares at \\_\\_\\_\\_. 'I'm not sending you to the invaders yet. I don't think you're ready. I want you to speak with an Arcanist, a Teir'Dal woman by the name of Aunrae V`Len, down south from here at Mu`Lin's Tower. You will recognize it by the wizard spires. She can tell you more about the assignment. Udra, safe travels.'\nCaptain Teiya says, 'In this case, some news is better than no news. At the very least, the information you provided is more knowledge regarding a threat to the area and the distraction to our soldiers. You did well. I may very well have more for you to do yet.'\n\n---\n\nCaptain Teiya of the Crystalwing regiment at Wyrmqueen's Ridge doesn't believe you are ready for information or requests regarding the invading draconic beings, but has Issued some orders for you to look into a matter to the south at Mu'Lin's Tower. Arcanist Aunrae V'Len will be your contact.\nThe first order of business is to check in with Arcanist Aunrae V'Len to see what the orders are about.\n1\\. Find and speak with Arcanist Aunrae V`Len 0/1 Hodstock Hills\nYou can find Arcanist Aunrae V`Len at the top of the tower in the south part of the zone at /way -2144, 478, 502\nYou say, 'Hail, Arcanist Aunrae V`Len'\nArcanist Aunrae V`Len says, 'Leave me.' She finally gets a good look at \\_\\_\\_\\_ and then purses her lips. 'You're here by order of [Captain Teiya], aren't you?'\nYou say, 'Captain Teiya sent me.'\nArcanist Aunrae V`Len says, 'Figures. I'd complain that she's interrupting my work, but she sent you here for said work.' On an aside, she mutters, 'Or at least some of it.' Smirking, she continues, 'So, welcome to my acquired tower, known as Mu`Lin's Tower, and for those a little more ancient than you or I, [Mu`Lin]'s Reach. It has handy access to and from the spire below, so I can avoid the excess walk, and it has a glorious view of why you're here: the [other towers].'\nYou say, 'Who is, or was, Mu`Lin?'\nArcanist Aunrae V`Len says, 'Mu`Lin was a powerful wizard who had discovered some of the teleportation magic in this area, through study of the runes and symbols local to this tower. I wouldn't doubt it if he's the man we should credit with us not losing a limb upon going through a portal.'\nYou say, 'What other towers?'\nYour task 'The Mysterious Towers' has been updated.\nArcanist Aunrae V`Len says, 'The towers across the way, atop the plateau. You can see them if you poke a look through the broken tower segment over there, eyes southwest. I need you to head over there and look for any signs of its origins, and the origin of the creatures within. Anything.'\n2\\. Observe the mysterious towers from atop Mu`Lin Tower 0/1 Hodstock Hills\nWalk to the ledge near Arcanist Aunrae V`Len, looking out of the tower. The step updates there.\n3\\. Explore the entrance to the mysterious towers 0/1 Hodstock Hills\nThis step updates at the tower in the southwestern part of the zone at /way -1398, 1909, 564\n4\\. Find a clue as to what happened at the towers 0/1 Hodstock Hills\nThis step updates when you pick up a ground spawn Noctix's Journal Page 1 at the top of the south ramp in the southwestern tower at /way -1882, 2196, 657 and you can find another one out on the catwalk on the top floor at /way -1655, 2342, 657\n5\\. Find a clue as to what happened at the towers 0/1 Hodstock Hills\nNoctix's Journal Page 4 is a ground spawn that can be found on the 2nd floor of the same tower near the ledge behind a pillar at /way -1420, 2296, 657\n6\\. Find a clue as to what happened at the towers 0/1 Hodstock Hills\nNoctix's Journal: Page 7 is a ground spawn on the ground floor in the same tower at /way -1854, 2303, 563\n7\\. Deliver Noctix's Journal: Page 1 to Arcanist Aunrae V`Len 0/1 Hodstock Hills\nYou offered 1 Noctix's Journal: Page 1 to Arcanist Aunrae V`Len.\n8\\. Deliver Noctix's Journal: Page 4 to Arcanist Aunrae V`Len 0/1 Hodstock Hills\nYou offered 1 Noctix's Journal: Page 4 to Arcanist Aunrae V`Len.\n9\\. Deliver Noctix's Journal: Page 7 to Arcanist Aunrae V`Len 0/1 Hodstock Hills\nYou offered 1 Noctix's Journal: Page 7 to Arcanist Aunrae V`Len.\nYour task 'The Mysterious Towers' has been updated.\nArcanist Aunrae V`Len yoinks the next page, reading through it quickly. 'Nightmare? Well, that's just rich.' She laughs out loud while reading the journal page. 'If he expected Terris Thule to want a slow-burn power-grab, he picked the wrong demi-goddess to please. Just ask her father.' Tapping her chin, she adds, 'Nightmare power certainly explains the restless nights previous adventurers described.'\nYour task 'The Mysterious Towers' has been updated.\nArcanist Aunrae V`Len takes and swiftly skims through page seven. 'And... there we go. Her little champion was too slow for her tastes. And he tries to appeal to a goddess with mushiness. Love. Ugh.'\nYour task 'The Mysterious Towers' has been updated.\nArcanist Aunrae V`Len takes hold of the first page and looks through it eagerly. The arcanist muses thoughtfully, 'So, they were a demi-planar power manifested for this guy, growing this lady goddess' power in the Material plane. Interesting...'\nYou complete the trade with Arcanist Aunrae V`Len.\n10\\. Check in with Arcanist Aunrae V`Len for the next step 0/1 Hodstock Hills\nYou say, 'Hail, Arcanist Aunrae V`Len'\nArcanist Aunrae V`Len seems rather amused with herself. 'So, let's review: It's a manifestation from the Demi-Plane of Nightmares, created by this Noctix-guy or by the goddess. A gift?' She shakes her head, disposing of the conjecture in support of the facts for the moment. 'He intended to use it to grow Terris' power, but his plan may have been too slow because he begged for her patience, and it's presently in a state of unsupervised lawlessness. Does that sound about [right]?'\nYou say, 'It's about as right as we can determine.'\nYour task 'The Mysterious Towers' has been updated.\nArcanist Aunrae V`Len says, 'Or is it...? I have a contact!' The realization certainly makes her perk up. 'Oh yes, yes, yes! You, my friend, are going on a field trip. I have a friend. An acquaintance, really. A contact! It's a business relationship. He's a nightmare in the Demi-Plane of Nightmares, going by the name of Therok. He's not aggressive, so you'll be fine if you can avoid those who are. Go and chat with him about Noctix and let me know what you find out.'\n11\\. Find Therok and ask him about Noctix 0/1 The Plane of Nightmare\nYou can find Therok in the underwater cave in the central northern part of Plane of Nightmare.\nYou say, 'Hail, Therok'\nTherok says, 'You [talk] me. What bring you?'\nYou say, 'Arcanist Aunrae V`Len sent me. I came to talk about Noctix.'\nTherok says, 'Oh! Mistress's [old champion].'\nYou say, 'Old champion? He was replaced?'\nTherok says, 'No. Champion gone though. Hero Realm? No? [Why] him?'\nYou say, 'The why is that we're looking into the towers created in Hodstock Hills near Mu`Lin's.'\nTherok says, 'Towers of Noctix! Towers of Bone! Towers no touch Nightmare many year. [Cut off].'\nYou say, 'It was cut off from this Demi-Plane?'\nTherok says, 'Yes. Yes. Long ago. Power down. Useless. Useless! Champion disappear [before] cut. Many friend there no talk me. Miss all friend. Miss all friend...'\nYou say, 'He disappeared before it lost contact with the Demi-Plane of Nightmares?'\nYour task 'The Mysterious Towers' has been updated.\nTherok says, 'No talk me. Go away. Remind of many friend. Remind of useless. Go away.'\n12\\. Let Arcanist Aunrae V`Len know how the discussion with Therok went 0/1 Hodstock Hills\nYou say, 'Hail, Arcanist Aunrae V`Len'\nArcanist Aunrae V`Len says, 'Did you find [Therok]? What did he say?'\nYou say, 'I found Therok.' The adventurer proceeds to share the information received. 'What do you make of it?'\nArcanist Aunrae V`Len says, 'Well, well. If they no longer have a connection with the Nightmare plane then theoretically we'll be able to reduce their numbers over time as they will die outside of the demi-plane's power. Want to [kill some] for me? For research, of course.'\nYou say, 'I will be happy to kill some nightmares.'\nYour task 'The Mysterious Towers' has been updated.\nArcanist Aunrae V`Len says, 'Excellent. Go! Go have fun. Get me a nice sample size.'\n13\\. Kill 6 nightmares within Towers of Noctix 0/6 Hodstock Hills\nThis is the tower in the southwest corner of the zone with all the undead. Kill any of the undead inside to update this step.\nHere are the mobs that counted for me on this step.\na decaying minion\na foul chanter\na frightener\ndespair\ndread\nmisery\ntribulation\n14\\. Let Arcanist Aunrae V`Len know the 'test' is complete 0/1 Hodstock Hills\nYou say, 'Hail, Arcanist Aunrae V`Len'\nYour task 'The Mysterious Towers' has been updated.\nArcanist Aunrae V`Len says, 'Well, they didn't remain dead, so I can only presume that despite being cut off, there's still some level of retained planar energy. This will take some more research. Sigh... Just as I was hoping on finally being able to really dig into my Mu`Lin transportation research. Go update Captain Teiya. I'll be here, I guess.'\n15\\. Report back to Captain Teiya 0/1 Hodstock Hills\nYou say, 'Hail, Captain Teiya'\nYour task 'The Mysterious Towers' has been updated.\nWhile the Towers of Noctix are no longer tied to the Plane of Nightmare, the powers within remain a threat to Hodstock and Freeport while the people are distracted with the greater threat of these otherworldly dragons.\nCaptain Teiya says, 'In this case, some news is better than no news. At the very least, the information you provided is more knowledge regarding a threat to the area and the distraction to our soldiers. You did well. I may very well have more for you to do yet.'\nYou light a firework.\nYou have successfully been granted your reward for: The Mysterious Towers\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\n267 platinum 1 gold 2 silver\nExperience\n**Submitted by:** Gidono",
