say, 'Let's take the fight to them.'\nCaptain Teiya says, 'Admittedly, we - as a force - have already started, but I would like for you to start Norrath-side. I have some requests for you.' The Captain gives a slight smirk and crosses her arms over her chest. 'It's not the most glamorous, but it's still important to the [cause].'\nYou say, 'I'll do whatever I can to help the cause.'\nYou have been assigned the task '...Is a Good Offense'.\nCaptain Teiya says, 'Good. Revol Aleslay here at Wyrmqueen's Ridge has been crafting all manner of equipment, including weaponry. I'd like to surprise him with some extra materials.' She hands \\_\\_\\_\\_ a paper with the small list of supplies on it. 'For the wood, there's bound to be one or two fallen fence posts that can be moved from in and around Hodstock Village. The best bet with the rope is to take it back from the bandits, as most of that belonged to Freeport from the start. Animal sinew should be self-explanatory on where to find that. The metal... see if our scalewrought visitors have any that might be of use. Go ahead and take them directly to him, and then let me know the reception.'\n\n---\n\nBased on your previous support of Hodstock Hills, Captain Teiya feels you have proved yourself and believes it's time for you to join the offensive against the Scale wrought forces Before you do, resupplying the weapons crafting effort is top priority.\nSome wood would be beneficial for Revol Aleslay, and you can find plenty of felled wooden fence posts within Hodstock Village proper. Not all fence posts would do for the work needed, but testing each of the felled fences can help narrow down the selection.\nCoiled rope would be extremely helpful for Revol Aleslay, and Captain Teiya believes the best source of rope would be the local bandits, as much of the rope they hold in their supplies were once Freeport's.\nAnimals are aplenty within Hodstock Hills, and sourced from the ground-based animals, their sinew can be used to craft items like bow strings. Bring a few to Revol Aleslay.\nIts expected that the scalewrought forces invading Norrath should have some metal that can be refined for weaponry. Collect some shards and bring them to Revol Aleslay.\n1\\. Find and deliver 1 Broken Fence Post to Revol Aleslay 0/1 Hodstock Hills\nBroken Fence Post is a ground spawn item that is found by clicking on the fence that is laying on the ground in Hodstock Village towards the center of the zone.\nHere are some spots that I was able to get Broken Fence Posts.\n/way -361, -71, -5\n/way -184, 66, -5\n/way -114, 196, -5\n/way -175, 140, -3\n/way 22, -39, -5\n/way -70, -118, -5\nThey respawn within a few minutes.\n2\\. Find and deliver 4 Coiled Ropes to Revol Aleslay 0/1 Hodstock Hills\nThese drop from bandits. It dropped 3 for the 3 people in my group with mercs.\n3\\. Find and deliver 4 Animal Sinew to Revol Aleslay 0/1 Hodstock Hills\nThese drop from animals. Badgers, bears and foxes drop this.\n4\\. Find and deliver 4 Metal Shards to Revol Aleslay 0/1 Hodstock Hills\nThese drop from scalewrought mobs.\n5\\. Check In with Revol Aleslay following the deliveries 0/1 Hodstock Hills\nYou say, 'Hail, Revol Aleslay'\nYour task '...Is a Good Offense' has been updated.\nRevol Aleslay takes a moment to look up from the sheer number of supplies brought to him, and smiles warmly. 'Oh, thanks, bud! This'll do very nicely, bud. Go ahead and tell 'em I appreciate it, will you?'\n6\\. Report back to Captain Teiya 0/1 Hodstock Hills\nYou say, 'Hail, Captain Teiya'\nYour task '...Is a Good Offense' has been updated.\nCaptain Teiya says, 'It's never a fun job, but you did it. Your work towards the defense of Norrath is appreciated. Now I have a new one for you.' She turns her head over her shoulder towards the two Crystalwing dragons presently overlooking the ridge, and despite them being difficult to make out from here, stealing glances towards the two platforms to either side of them. 'I'd like for you to check in with the twins, Torin and Olmnoth, regarding the departure and arrival procedures. We're going to send you to the leviathan, and I want to make sure you know how to safely get there.'\n7\\. Speak with Torin regarding the departure platform 0/1 Hodstock Hills\nTorin is at /way 970, 1708, 463 at the south end of the quest givers camp with a griffin next to him.\nYou say, 'Hail, Torin'\nYour task '...Is a Good Offense' has been updated.\nTorin says, 'Oh, heya, vasha. I'm Torin, a handler of the griffins here at Wyrmqueen's Ridge. If you need to head up to the leviathan, I'll be the guy to talk to. I'm guessing Captain Teiya sent you.' He smiles warmly with an understanding nod. 'That means we're sending more people above.' That warm smile immediately starts to fade. 'On one hand, the griffins have been restless and will appreciate the work. On the other hand... Well, you should chat with my brother Olmnoth. He's over at the arrival platform.'\n8\\. Speak with Olmnoth regarding the arrival platform 0/1 Hodstock Hills\nOlmnoth is at /way 1487, 1727, 441, just north of Torin.\nYou say, 'Hail, Olmnoth'\nYour task '...Is a Good Offense' has been updated.\nOlmnoth says, 'Vasha and salutations.' His eyes narrow, not quite displaying the same warm reception as his twin brother at the departure platform. 'Well, we're finally sending people back up there? I wonder if that means we're giving up on those we sent before.' He purses his lips. 'Captain Teiya didn't tell you, did she? It figures. No one who has been sent to the leviathan has returned yet. Trust me. Standing here, I would know. You should ask her about it. Then again, that's probably why she sent you to us, for us to be the bearers of bad news.' He looks over to the arrival platform. 'Well, presuming people, and griffins, start returning, they will land here. So keep it clear. Understood? Good.'\n9\\. Update Captain Teiya on the status 0/1 Hodstock Hills\nYou say, 'Hail, Captain Teiya'\nYour task '...Is a Good Offense' has been updated.\nCaptain Teiya says, 'So you've received the warning. It's true, no one has returned yet, so if you are all in on this as I expect you are, you'll need to go in with that understanding that once you're there, you're on your own unless and until you find members of the previous party. On that note...' She straightens, bringing her feet together. 'Should you not back out of travel, you are to find and report to Mokolin as soon as possible. We can only assume she is still alive.' After a deep breath, she continues, 'It's time to go, if you're ready. Talk to Torin again to travel. Stay safe. Udra.'\n10\\. Report to Mokolin on the great leviathan 0/1 The Theater of Eternity\nMokolin is at the zone in to The Theater Eternity at /way -8, -308, -1. To get to The Theater of Eternity, talk to Torin to get on the griffon which will zone you over.\nYou say, 'Hail, Mokolin'\nYour task '...Is a Good Offense' has been updated.\nYou discovered Mokolin is still alive, and transport to the Theater of Eternity aboard the leviathan is now possible for you.\nMokolin blinks in surprise at the presence of a new friendly face, momentarily speechless.\nYou have successfully been granted your reward for: ...Is a Good Offense\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\n267 platinum 1 gold 2 silver\nExperience\n**Submitted by:** Gidono",
